"## 2026-11-21-dependency-and-ci-debts — Dependency Security: 4 row(s)\n**Section:** Dependency Security\n**Change:** ~ decision/skia-default-build-fetch · rule: was «Skia is built by default in the browser app and the WPT runner, its build script fetching prebuilt binaries from GitHub releases at build time with no content check.»; now «Skia is built by default in the browser app and the WPT runner from a prebuilt archive for the locked skia-bindings tag, fetched once per platform and verified against a committed per-target sha256; a differing archive is refused, leaving no file, and the build reads only the verified local copy.»\n~ decision/dependency-audit-cargo-deny · except: was «`unsound` stays at its default, which keeps memmap2's unsound advisory out of the gate.»; now «`unsound` stays at its default, which keeps memmap2's unsound advisory out of the gate, a wait on a cacache release as cacache 13.1.0 uses no advise_range.»\n+ decision/skia-archive-fallback-source-build — Skia archive fallback stated as a limit\n+ decision/no-force-skia-binaries-download — No forced skia binaries download\n**Why:** decision/skia-default-build-fetch: The build-time fetch is no longer unchecked: the archive is verified against a committed sha256 record before the build reads it, so the row's «with no content check» is false.\ndecision/dependency-audit-cargo-deny: The memmap2 exception now carries its stated outcome, a wait on a cacache release, which the row's except leaves out.\ndecision/skia-archive-fallback-source-build: The chunk states the skia archive fallback as a limit read red by a witness, a decision no row holds.\ndecision/no-force-skia-binaries-download: The planned forced download was measured to give a source build and dropped, a deliberate choice no row states.\n**Ref:** .andromeda/runs/2026-11-22T02-02-17-wrap/",
"## 2026-11-21-dependency-and-ci-debts — Secret Management: 1 row(s)\n**Section:** Secret Management\n**Change:** + contract/environment-variables/skia-binaries-url — Environment variables · SKIA_BINARIES_URL\n**Why:** contract/environment-variables/skia-binaries-url: The chunk adds an environment variable set by CI and read by a build script, and the environment-variable contract lists none for it.\n**Ref:** .andromeda/runs/2026-11-22T02-02-17-wrap/",
